---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Responsible Gambling Resources"
  description="Support resources, helplines, and information for anyone experiencing gambling-related problems or seeking help."
>
  <Hero
    title="Gambling Support Resources"
    subtitle="Help Is Available If You Need It"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            If gambling has stopped being entertainment and started causing problems in your life, support is available. This page provides resources for anyone seeking help—whether for yourself or someone you care about. These organizations offer confidential assistance without judgment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="National Resources" id="national">
        <div class="resource-card">
          <h3>National Council on Problem Gambling</h3>
          <p><strong>Helpline:</strong> 1-800-522-4700 (24/7, confidential)</p>
          <p><strong>Text:</strong> 1-800-522-4700</p>
          <p><strong>Chat:</strong> <a href="https://www.ncpgambling.org/chat" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ncpgambling.org/chat</a></p>
          <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.ncpgambling.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ncpgambling.org</a></p>
          <p>The primary national resource for problem gambling support, offering free confidential help 24 hours a day.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-card">
          <h3>Gamblers Anonymous</h3>
          <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.gamblersanonymous.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gamblersanonymous.org</a></p>
          <p>A fellowship of people who share their experience, strength, and hope with each other to recover from gambling addiction.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-card">
          <h3>National Problem Gambling Helpline Network</h3>
          <p><strong>Call or Text:</strong> 1-800-522-4700</p>
          <p>Connects callers to local resources and provides immediate support regardless of location.</p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Warning Signs" id="warning-signs">
        <p>Consider seeking help if you experience:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Betting more than you can afford to lose</li>
          <li>Needing to bet larger amounts for the same excitement</li>
          <li>Trying to win back losses by gambling more</li>
          <li>Lying about gambling to family or friends</li>
          <li>Borrowing money or selling possessions to gamble</li>
          <li>Neglecting work, relationships, or responsibilities</li>
          <li>Feeling restless or irritable when trying to stop</li>
          <li>Gambling to escape problems or negative feelings</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <Callout type="info" title="Help Is Confidential">
        <p>
          All resources listed provide confidential support. Reaching out is the hardest step—the people at these organizations understand and are ready to help without judgment.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <ContentSection title="Self-Exclusion Programs" id="self-exclusion">
        <p>
          Most states offer self-exclusion programs that allow you to voluntarily ban yourself from casinos and sportsbooks. Contact your state's gaming commission for information about local programs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Many online sportsbooks also offer self-exclusion, deposit limits, and cooling-off periods. These tools can be accessed through account settings or by contacting customer support.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="For Friends and Family" id="family">
        <p>
          If someone you care about is struggling with gambling:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Gam-Anon:</strong> Support groups for family and friends of problem gamblers — <a href="https://www.gam-anon.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gam-anon.org</a></li>
          <li>The NCPG helpline also provides support for those affected by someone else's gambling</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Remember" id="remember">
        <p>
          Problem gambling is treatable. Many people recover with appropriate support. Seeking help is a sign of strength, not weakness. If gambling is causing problems in your life, please reach out to one of these resources.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .resource-card { background-color: var(--color-surface); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg); }
  .resource-card h3 { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); color: var(--color-text); }
  .resource-card p { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .resource-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .resource-card a { color: var(--color-accent); }
</style>
